#~
A line read from a FIFO returns when the line is complete, so the reader can answer it.

Driven by run_vm_flag_tests.py (check_fifo_line_ack), POSIX only: the driver makes two
FIFOs, writes to <data> and reads <ack>.

A FileReader looked one byte ahead after opening a file and after every line, so that
IsEoF() is true as soon as the last line has been read. On a FIFO the byte it looked for
is the writer's NEXT message. A writer that sends "ready\n", keeps the FIFO open and waits
for an acknowledgment before it writes again never got one: ReadLine had its line and was
waiting in the look ahead, so the program could not send the acknowledgment (Codex review
round 3, slice E, finding 5). A handle that can wait is no longer looked ahead at; the
end of a FIFO is found by the read that meets it, as on a pipe or a socket.

  (no argument)          print PASS, so the regression runner can run this file
  <data> <ack> line      the driver has written "ready\n" already: read it, acknowledge
                         it on <ack>, and read the "done\n" the driver sends only then
  <data> <ack> open      the driver has written nothing: say "hello" on <ack> as soon as
                         <data> is open, which the driver waits for before it writes at
                         all; then as "line"
~#
use System.IO.Filesystem;

class FifoLineAck {
  function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
    if(args->Size() < 3) {
      "PASS: fifo_line_ack"->PrintLine();
      return;
    };

    reader := FileReader->New(args[0]);
    answers := FileWriter->New(args[1]);
    if(args[2]->Equals("open")) {
      answers->WriteString("hello\n");
      answers->Flush();
    };

    first := reader->ReadLine();
    answers->WriteString("ack\n");
    answers->Flush();

    second := reader->ReadLine();
    third := reader->ReadLine();
    reader->Close();
    answers->Close();

    at_end := third = Nil;
    "first='{$first}' second='{$second}' end={$at_end}"->PrintLine();
    if(first <> Nil & first->Equals("ready") & second <> Nil & second->Equals("done") & third = Nil) {
      "PASS: fifo_line_ack protocol"->PrintLine();
    }
    else {
      "FAIL: the lines read from the FIFO are not the ones written"->PrintLine();
      Runtime->Exit(1);
    };
  }
}
